<title>NEW ZEALAND: Power NZ profit, pre-abnormals, rises 20 pct.</title>
<headline>Power NZ profit, pre-abnormals, rises 20 pct.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1996-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>Net profit (before abnormals)  55.32 vs 46.14</p>
<p>Note - Net profit after non-recurring items, minorities and equity earnings fell to NZ$51.12 million from $64.95 million. The prior-year bottom line number was inflated by the sale of Power NZ's stake in Wellington's EnergyDirect.  </p>
<p>    Shr (cents, pre-abnormals)	    33.8 vs 32.1</p>
<p>    Div (cents)				 14.0 vs 25.9</p>
<p>    Total div for yr (cents)		25.0 vs 35.1</p>
<p>    Turnover				  385.03 vs 302.40</p>
<p>    Abnormals			  debit  0.03 vs credit 16.34</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			    81.99 vs 83.16</p>
<p>    Tax					  26.60 vs 20.68</p>
<p>    Equity earnings (loss)		  2.03 vs (profit) 2.47</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (million)	151.47 vs same</p>
<p>Dividend carries full imputation credit.</p>
<p>Pay date July 27</p>
<p>Registration and ex date to be advised.</p>
<p>Note - Power New Zealand Ltd is New Zealand's largest listed Power distributor. The company's largest shareholders are UtiliCorp New Zealand Ltd, a unit of Kansas-based UtiliCorp United Inc and unlisted Mercury Energy Ltd.</p>
</text>
